From ab6de9d82747b82fba5749c84ea08fd63ceaf083 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yichongt <yichong.tang@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 15:39:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Add static LLM seq_len padding via --llm-lang-tokens

Allow exporting OV with a fixed LLM seq_len: --llm-lang-tokens specifies the
language-token reserve; total static seq_len = lang + captured visual tokens.
LLM, VL self-attention and DiT (and the single-OV pipeline) all bake this length
in, and inference zero-pads the input up to it, so different prompt lengths
share one static-shape OV compilation.

To avoid padding tokens contaminating the rest of the sequence, VL self-attention
is exported through a thin wrapper that consumes an attention_mask. DiT image/
backbone masks are padded as False so the diffusion pass already ignores padded
slots.

Verified on LIBERO_PANDA: split-OV padded vs baseline give cosine=1.0 / MAE=0;
single-OV padded vs PyTorch matches the baseline OV-vs-PyTorch numbers exactly
(trimmed cosine=0.999984, max_abs=0.010), so padding introduces no extra error.
